    "q": "Is Mardi Himal Trek suitable for beginners?",
    "a": "Mardi Himal is rated Moderate. It's achievable for first-timers with a reasonable level of fitness, but it's a step up from an easy trek. Day 4 starts at 4:30 AM and involves reaching 4,000m, which requires acclimatisation and stamina. If you can handle 5–7 hours of walking on consecutive days, including some steep sections, you'll be fine. We include an acclimatisation hike on Day 3 to help your body adjust."
