  <div class="about-text plan-section">
        <span class="section-label">Plan Your Trek</span>
        <h2 class="content-title">Best Time, Cost and Getting There</h2>
        <div class="title-divider"></div>
        <p><strong>Best time:</strong> October and November give the clearest views and dry trails, and March to May brings rhododendron blooms through the forest. December is quiet and clear but cold at High Camp. June to September is monsoon, when the high ridge gets slippery and views are unpredictable.</p>
        <p><strong>Cost:</strong> the trek costs $360 to $410 per person depending on group size. It includes private transport, meals, tea house accommodation, guide and porter, and the ACAP permit. See the cost table.</p>
        <p><strong>Getting there:</strong> we drive from Pokhara to Kande in about an hour and start walking from there. The trek ends at Siding village, with a jeep back to Pokhara in a couple of hours.</p>
        <p><strong>Mardi Himal or Kokhe Danda?</strong> If you want an easier trek with family-run homestays and village life instead of high camps, try the <a href="/kokhe-danda-trek">Kokhe Danda Trek</a>, the highest point of Parbat district. Want more viewpoints in one trip? See the <a href="/multiple-viewpoints-trek">Multiple Viewpoints Trek</a>.</p>
      </div>

